The MLX implementation in `src/mlx_tsfm/models/timesfm.py` is a port/translation
of the reference `timesfm3` PyTorch implementation from that project. The model
architecture and algorithms (patch featurization, iterative running-stats RevIN,
linear detrending, RoPE, per-dim-scale QK-norm attention, sequence + variate
mixing, patch stitching, and CPM RevIN refinement) originate there.

Changes made: reimplemented in Apple MLX for inference on Apple Silicon;
numerically verified against the reference implementation (max abs error ~1e-6).

TimesFM model weights (e.g. google/timesfm-3.0-pytorch) are distributed by Google
under a separate, non-commercial license and are NOT included in or redistributed
by this repository; they are downloaded by the user at runtime.
